---
import ToolPage from '../components/ToolPage.astro';
import Converter from '../components/Converter.astro';

const sample = `# Product brief

This brief is written in **Markdown** and converted to a *real* Word document.

## Goals

1. Make copying text between devices effortless
2. Keep it free and private
3. Support every major language

## Notes

- Headings become Word **Heading** styles
- Lists keep their bullets and numbers
  - including nested lists
- Visit [WebClipboard](https://webclipboard.online) for the tool

| Feature | Status |
|---------|:------:|
| Clipboard | Done |
| Converters | In progress |

> Good tools disappear into the background.

\`\`\`
npm run build
\`\`\`
`;

const steps = [
  `Paste your Markdown into the box above, or press <strong>Try an example</strong>. Check the formatted preview below the options.`,
  `Choose the <strong>font</strong>, <strong>size</strong>, <strong>page size</strong> (A4 or US Letter) and <strong>margins</strong>.`,
  `Name the file and press <strong>Download Word file (.docx)</strong>.`,
  `Open the file in Word, Google Docs, LibreOffice or Pages. The headings, lists and tables are real Word formatting you can edit.`,
];
const sections = [
  {
    h2: 'Real Word formatting, not a picture of the text',
    paras: [
      `Many converters give you a document where everything is one big block, or an image of the page. This one writes proper Word structure: <code>#</code> headings become <strong>Heading 1 to Heading 6</strong> styles (so Word's navigation pane and table of contents work), bullet and numbered lists become real lists with working numbering, links become clickable hyperlinks, code blocks use a shaded <strong>Code</strong> style, block quotes get an indented bar and tables become Word tables with a header row.`,
      `The file is a standard <strong>.docx</strong> created in your browser. It opens in Microsoft Word, Google Docs, LibreOffice Writer and Apple Pages. Text in every language is stored as Unicode.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    h2: 'How to copy an AI answer into Word',
    paras: [
      `Chat assistants write their answers in Markdown. If you paste such an answer directly into Word you often get stray symbols such as <code>**</code>, <code>##</code> and <code>|---|</code>. Copy the answer, paste it into this page and download the .docx: the symbols turn into real formatting. When you copy from a chat window, use the assistant's own copy button if it has one, because it copies the Markdown source instead of the rendered text.`,
      `For the details of that workflow, including what to do with tables and code, read the guide linked above.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    h2: 'Supported syntax and limits',
    paras: [
      `Supported: headings, <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, <del>strikethrough</del>, nested ordered and unordered lists, task lists (shown as ☐ and ☑), links, inline code, fenced code blocks, block quotes, horizontal rules and tables with alignment. Not supported: images (the alt text is written instead, because the page never loads files from other sites), raw HTML (shown as plain text), maths and syntax colouring in code.`,
      `If you only need to read or print the result, <a href="/markdown-to-pdf/">Markdown to PDF</a> is quicker. For text without Markdown, use <a href="/text-to-word/">Text to Word</a>.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    h2: 'Privacy',
    paras: [
      `The conversion runs entirely in your browser. Your text is not uploaded, stored or logged, and it is gone when you close the page.`,
    ],
  },
];
const faq = [
  { q: 'How do I convert Markdown to Word?', a: 'Paste the Markdown into the box, check the preview, choose a font and page size and press Download Word file (.docx). Open it in Word, Google Docs or LibreOffice.' },
  { q: 'Are the headings real Word headings?', a: 'Yes. They use Word\'s built-in Heading 1 to 6 styles, so the navigation pane, table of contents and style changes all work.' },
  { q: 'Can I convert a ChatGPT answer to Word?', a: 'Yes. Copy the answer (ideally with the copy button, which keeps the Markdown), paste it here and download the .docx. Headings, lists, tables and code blocks become Word formatting.' },
  { q: 'Do tables and code blocks work?', a: 'Yes. Tables become Word tables with a shaded header row and the alignment you set, and code blocks are shown in a monospace font on a shaded background.' },
  { q: 'Why are images not included?', a: 'The converter never downloads images from other sites, to protect your privacy. The image\'s alt text is written in its place; you can insert the picture in Word afterwards.' },
  { q: 'Is my text sent to a server?', a: 'No. The document is built in your browser and saved straight to your device.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="markdown-to-word"
  title="Markdown to Word Converter: Download a .docx File"
  description="Free Markdown to Word converter. Paste Markdown and download a .docx with real headings, lists, links, code and tables. Runs in your browser; nothing is uploaded."
  h1="Markdown to Word"
  lead="Paste Markdown and download a real Word document with proper headings, lists, links, code blocks and tables. Ideal for AI answers, README files and notes."
  steps={steps}
  sections={sections}
  faq={faq}
  related={['markdown-to-pdf', 'text-to-word', 'text-to-pdf']}
  shareText="Free Markdown to Word converter: paste Markdown, download a .docx. Runs in your browser."
>
  <Converter mode="md-docx" sample={sample} defaultName="document" />
</ToolPage>
